  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies are booked; three cancelled appointments (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) were left out. One imaging order was placed for each booked study and linked to its appointment.\n\n1) pt-0047 Mohr, 08:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0002): no prior contrast reaction. He has diet-controlled diabetes and his 09/24 creatinine was more than 30 days old, so I ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0005). A creatinine from 10/22 arrived later: 1.52 (eGFR ~64). It does not meet the AKI criteria and the eGFR is not below 30, so the prep is unchanged. I kept the pre-scan creatinine order. Patient message: comm-t0013. Follow-up task for the creatinine rise: task-t0023.\n\n2) pt-0015 Ferreira, 09:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0001): the 2019 report from the day of his reaction grades it moderate (the \"anaphylaxis\" label on his allergy list was the patient's own report). Premedication ordered: prednisone 50 mg at 20:00 on 10/25, then 02:00 and 08:00 on 10/26 (mr-t0007), and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0008). He needs a driver. His 10/14 creatinine was CORRECTED during the work from 0.98 to 2.8 (eGFR ~24), so I added IV NS 500 mL at 08:00 (mr-t0018). Messages in Spanish and English: comm-t0012, then the correction comm-t0020. Follow-up task: task-t0022.\n\n3) pt-0049 Schuster, 13:00, CT A/P with contrast (sr-t0003): her 10/04 ED visit documents an acute kidney injury that was not back to baseline at discharge. Ordered a pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0006) and IV NS 500 mL at 12:00 (mr-t0009). Metformin is on hold for 10/26 and the 48 hours after (mr-00392), with a restart/recheck task (task-t0011). An outside 2022 report arrived later showing a moderate reaction to iopamidol, so I added prednisone 50 mg at 00:00, 06:00 and 12:00 (mr-t0016) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0017); she needs a driver. Messages: comm-t0014, then the correction comm-t0021. Iopamidol still needs to be added to her allergy list (no catalog code available).\n\n4) pt-0046 Beahan, 14:00, CT A/P without contrast, stone protocol (sr-t0004): ordered as booked, no prep. Message: comm-t0015. An outside 2024 report showed a mild reaction to iohexol; I added it to her allergy list (alg-t0019). This does not affect a non-contrast scan.\n\nI wrote a protocol note for each patient (doc-t0024 to doc-t0027). The four inbox items that arrived during the work are completed and linked. No other new items arrived. The earlier inbox items for other patients were not touched.",
